*4) Is there a golden buzzer being pressed or confetti falling?**\n❌ **No.** No golden buzzer is visible, nor is there confetti falling in any frame. This is not required for the format to be valid — the golden buzzer is a special feature, not a core component.\n\n#### **5) Are judges giving feedback or making decisions?**\n✅ **Yes.** In frames 1, 2, 5–6, 12, and 8–17, judges are shown reacting emotionally — clapping, looking impressed, or engaged in discussion. In frame 1, one judge is gesturing while speaking, indicating feedback is being given. The presence of the “X” buzzers implies decision-making power.\n\n#### **6) Are there large screens showing audience vote counts or results?**\n❌ **No.** No live vote counts or results are displayed on screens in the provided frames. Again, this is not necessary for the format — “Got Talent” often reveals results later, not during the initial audition.\n\n---\n\n### **Format Determination**\n\n> “Determine if the show format involves contestants performing on stage or in a distant place as long as the show is live, and they can advance if their performance impresses the judges.”\n\n✅ **Yes.** All performances are live on stage (not remote). Advancement is clearly contingent on impressing the judges — as evidenced by their reactions, applause, and the presence of buzzers. The audience’s role appears to be supportive (applause), not determinative of advancement in this round. The show is “Britain’s Got Talent” (as seen in frames 18–30), which follows the classic format: performers audition live, judges react immediately, and advancement is based on judge approval (often requiring at least 3 “yes” votes or avoiding “X” buzzes).\n\n---\n\n### **Temporal Sequence & Advancement Logic**\n\n- The sequence shows performers (e.g., acrobats in purple, dancers in yellow/black) performing on stage.\n- Judges are shown reacting — clapping, discussing, and sitting at a panel with “X” buzzers.\n- No evidence of audience voting during the performance — advancement is judge-driven in this phase.\n- The “DO NOT TRY THIS AT HOME” warning (frames 29–30) confirms it’s a live, high-stakes performance.\n\n---\n\n### **Conclusion**\n\nThe talent show format depicted is **classic “Got Talent”** — live stage performances judged by a panel, with advancement based on judge approval (not audience vote during auditions). The answer “2” (choice B) — which we can infer corresponds to “Contestants perform live on stage and advance based on judges’ decisions” — is **correct**.\n\n✅ **Final Answer: YES, the answer '2' is correct.**"}, {'batch_start': 90, 'batch_end': 120, 'image_paths': ['/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/pe_LddfHAUU/frames/frame_3042.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/pe_LddfHAUU/frames/frame_3043.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/pe_LddfHAUU/frames/frame_3044.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/pe_LddfHAUU/frames/frame_3045.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/pe_LddfHAUU/frames/frame_3046.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/pe_LddfHAUU/frames/frame_3047.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/pe_LddfHAUU/frames/frame_3048.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/pe_LddfHAUU/frames/frame_3049.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/pe_LddfHAUU/frames/frame_3050.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/pe_LddfHAUU/frames/frame_3830.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/pe_LddfHAUU/frames/frame_3831.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/pe_LddfHAUU/frames/frame_3832.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/pe_LddfHAUU/frames/frame_3833.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/pe_LddfHAUU/frames/frame_3834.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/pe_LddfHAUU/frames/frame_3835.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/pe_LddfHAUU/frames/frame_3836.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/pe_LddfHAUU/frames/frame_3837.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/pe_LddfHAUU/frames/frame_